<title>FRANCE: New York top May Paris import air cargo generator.</title>
<headline>New York top May Paris import air cargo generator.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top airport gateway for airfreight imports to Charles de Gaulle and Orly airports in May 1997.</p>
<p>The top 10 airport gateways for ADP air cargo imports in May 1997 and, in parentheses, the percentage change on May 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p>  1.  New York	2,794 tonnes	    (-5.7 percent)</p>
<p>  2.  Chicago	 2,213 tonnes	    (-1.5)</p>
<p>  3.  Tokyo	   1,620 tonnes	   (+29.3)</p>
<p>  4.  Hong Kong     1,516 tonnes	   (+17.6)</p>
<p>  5.  Los Angeles   1,153 tonnes	   (-14.4)</p>
<p>  6.  Montreal	1,009 tonnes	   (-11.2)</p>
<p>  7.  Singapore	 758 tonnes	  (+142.5)</p>
<p>  8.  Taipei	    633 tonnes	   (+46.9)</p>
<p>  9.  Miami	     533 tonnes	   (-23.7)</p>
<p>  10. Seoul	     484 tonnes	    (+1.9)</p>
<p>-Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel +44 171 542 7706;  Fax +5017</p>
